<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 488)</h2>
<p><b>A stand-in that can't be used now says so.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>Optimized media that exists but can't be used is marked in the playlist</b> with a struck-through bolt, and the shot says why when you land on it. Until now a refused stand-in was silent: the shot simply played at full resolution off the studio volume, and the only symptom was that everything felt slow for no visible reason.</li>
<li>A stand-in is refused when its source has been re-rendered since, or when it was encoded from a different color space than the shot now declares. Both mean re-optimizing that shot.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
